      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "BLOOD RED (5) finds the maiden win elusive but it certainly hasn't been without trying. Has run well here and profiles strongly in this line-up. JOSEPHINE OF TUFFY (2) has been fourth at her past two runs at this track, with the latest made tougher by racing wide from the 1000m, and her placed record at the track and distance keeps her right in the mix. PAINTED WINGS (4) is another honest maiden rather than a winner to trust blindly, yet consecutive thirds at this venue and a last-start effort with interference make her a live threat if the quick back-up and first attempt around 1890m are handled. MISS CHAMONIX (6) has been improving and will appreciate the rise in trip fourth-up. Could take some holding out down in the weights. TRUSTY FELINA (1) has been doing her best work late in her first two starts. Can play a more significant role third-up with the sharp rise in trip.",
